# Entries added by the ConjureRhyme fork, in cmudict.dict's own line format.
#
# Full-line comments (like this one) and blank lines are stripped by
# apply-additions.py. Everything else is copied verbatim, so an entry here is
# byte-for-byte what lands in cmudict.dict.
#
# Rules for adding to this file:
#
#   - The base head word must already exist upstream. This file adds
#     *pronunciations*, not vocabulary; a genuinely missing word is a different
#     kind of change and wants a different justification.
#   - Cite the analogous upstream entries that set the pattern. Every addition
#     here should be defensible as "upstream already does this, one word over".
#   - Do not reorder. A variant is inserted after the last existing variant of
#     its base, which is where upstream puts them.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# transplant: the noun is missing
#
# Upstream has only the verb, tranSPLANT (T R AE0 N S P L AE1 N T). English
# stress-shifts this Latinate trans- family between verb and noun, and upstream
# already records both halves for the two closest analogues:
#
#     transfer     T R AE0 N S F ER1        transport     T R AE0 N S P AO1 R T
#     transfer(2)  T R AE1 N S F ER0        transport(2)  T R AE1 N S P AO0 R T
#     transfers    T R AE0 N S F ER1 Z      transports    T R AE0 N S P AO1 R T S
#     transfers(2) T R AE1 N S F ER0 Z      transports(2) T R AE1 N S P AO0 R T S
#
# The noun is the commoner sense by far ("marrow transplant", "heart
# transplant"), and with only the verb recorded those phrases come out as
# 1001 rather than 1010. The two lines below are the transfer/transport
# template applied to transplant, and the plural carries the variant for the
# same reason transports(2) does.
transplant(2) T R AE1 N S P L AE0 N T
transplants(2) T R AE1 N S P L AE0 N T S
